{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "F24RecurrenceDroppedOnThePipelinePath",
  "description": "FINDING F24 — a causal self-reference is SILENTLY DROPPED on the build-pipeline evaluation path: every self-read comes back unresolved, and any clamp in the body launders it into a plausible number.\n\nWHAT THE DOCUMENT SAYS. `s[1] = 1`, `s[k] = 2 x s[k-1]`, i.e. [1, 2, 4, 8]: esm-spec §4.3.1.1's canonical spelling, an equation whose LHS is an array-shaped unknown and whose `aggregate` body reads `index(s, k - 1)`, itself, strictly earlier along its own output axis.\n\nWHAT THE TWO PATHS DO WITH IT.\n\n    esm test <this file>      ->  [1, 2, 4, 8]   correct; the four assertions pass\n    esm simulate <this file>  ->  [1, 0, 0, 0]   every self-read read as zero\n\nSo this document's inline test PASSES and is not the repro. The repro is the DISAGREEMENT, and run-tests.sh checks it by running both commands — an inverted check, like the one F19 had: it fails when `simulate` starts agreeing, because that means the defect is fixed and the workarounds it forces are dead weight.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS HERE RATHER THAN BEING A CLI CURIOSITY. `run_simulate` turns the build pipeline on for a relational document, and turns it on unconditionally for a document that INGESTS (`popts.build_pipeline = true` whenever providers exist). Two consequences for this port. A fixture's emitted answer goes through `esm simulate`, so a recurrence can never reach `MOVESOutput`; and a fixture that reads `data_sources` is on the pipeline path even under `esm test`, so its own inline assertions are computed the broken way too. That is why fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm still CARRIES agedist.f's fold while components/age_distribution.esm, which does not ingest, computes it and asserts it in 55 places.\n\nCONFIRMED UPSTREAM, NOT A SPELLING PROBLEM HERE. The repro is EarthSciAST's own canonical valid example, ../EarthSciAST/tests/valid/recurrence_causal_self_reference.esm: `esm test` gives 6/6, and `esm simulate --observed r` gives that file's non-recurrent `b[y]` const verbatim, [1e-16, 1, 1e-16, 1e8, 3, -1e16], meaning the self-read term contributed nothing at all. Four spellings were tried before filing: the bare-variable LHS, the §4.3 indexed-aggregate LHS (`aggregate{expr: s[k]} ~ …`, the other form §4.3.1.1's Recognition paragraph admits), a one-axis fold and a two-axis fold with the second axis an identity index. All four evaluate correctly under `esm test` and in all four the self-read comes back unresolved under `esm simulate`.\n\nTHE FAILURE MODE IS THE ONE THIS REPOSITORY FEARS MOST. Nothing is rejected, nothing is logged, and CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.19.4 requires the opposite — an unavailable self-read is `E_TREEWALK_RECUR_UNAVAILABLE` and MUST NOT resolve to a number, precisely because a clamp such as the `max(x, 0)` in agedist.f's own body launders the substituted zero into a plausible number and then feeds it to every later cell. Measured on this port: with the fold wired into the fixture, `fold_totalPopulation` at 1991 came out as 1e-4 x (1 + grwfac) instead of 83.3 x (1 + grwfac) — the signature of `max(self_read, MINGRWIND)` with a zero self-read — and the grown fractions summed to 1.5e-06 instead of 4.697819.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "finding",
   "recurrence",
   "aggregate",
   "silent",
   "two-path"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "step_rows": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 4
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "F24RecurrenceDroppedOnThePipelinePath": {
   "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-12
   },
   "variables": {
    "s_value": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "step_rows"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 at the first step, twice the previous value at every later one. The shape of agedist.f's year fold with everything but the self-reference removed, and exactly esm-spec §4.3.1.1's worked example. [1, 2, 4, 8] on the scalar path; [1, 0, 0, 0] on the pipeline path, where 0 is what the unresolved self-read returns."
    },
    "s_clamped": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "step_rows"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "description": "The same recurrence with a CLAMP in its body, which is the shape agedist.f actually has: `s[1] = 1`, `s[k] = 2 x max(s[k-1], 0) + 1`, i.e. [1, 3, 7, 15]. On the pipeline path the unresolved self-read is NaN and `max(NaN, 0)` returns 0, so this column reads [1, 1, 1, 1] -- a plausible, finite, monotone-looking answer with no diagnostic anywhere. `s_value` next to it is the unclamped control that reads NaN instead. The pair is the whole of CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.19.4's argument for why a NaN sentinel is not sufficient and the fault must be raised."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "s_value",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "step_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "k",
          1
         ]
        },
        1.0,
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "s_value",
            {
             "op": "-",
             "args": [
              "k",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          2.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "s_clamped",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "step_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "k",
          1
         ]
        },
        1.0,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "max",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "s_clamped",
                {
                 "op": "-",
                 "args": [
                  "k",
                  1
                 ]
                }
               ]
              },
              0.0
             ]
            },
            2.0
           ]
          },
          1.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "the_recurrence_evaluates_on_the_scalar_path",
     "description": "This PASSES, and its passing is half the finding. `esm test` builds without the pipeline for a document that does not ingest, and on that path the construct works exactly as specified. run-tests.sh asserts the other half by command: that `esm simulate` on this same file still disagrees. The two values are 4 and 8 rather than 1 and 2 because the doubling has to have compounded: a path that resolved only the FIRST self-read to zero would still give 1 at step 1.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.0
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "s_value",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 1.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 1
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "s_value",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 2.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 2
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "s_value",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 4.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 3
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "s_value",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 8.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 4
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "s_clamped",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 1.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 1
       }
      },
      {
